# Push changes to GitHub

After you create or edit files in this repo, commit that work and push it to GitHub on the current branch, including `main`.

Do this for every change you make. Skip the commit or the push only when the user says not to in that request.

Keep the usual git safety limits: do not commit secrets, do not force-push, do not skip hooks, and do not change git config.
